senses.gloss:
आक्रांत p. p.
1 Seized, taken
possession of, overpowered, defeated,
vanquished, overcome;
आक्रांतविमानमार्गं R. 13. 37 reaching upto; रुजा˚
Pt. 5. 52; दिदृक्षा˚ हृदयः Dk. 141
seized with; आतपाक्रांतोयमुद्देशः
M. 3 exposed to heat;
आक्रांतपूर्वमिव भुजंगं R. 9. 79 trodden or
trampled under foot; filled with,
full of, occupied, covered,
overspread; शुशुभे तेन चाक्रांतं मंगलायतनं
महत् R. 17. 29; Bh. 2. 108;
वलिभिर्मुखमाक्रांतं Bh. 3. 14, 62; U. 2. 20;
Mv. 5. 40; Śi. 1. 70; H. 1. 24; Dk. 141;
K. 55; Ve. 2. 26; ˚मति having the
mind engrossed or occupied;
U. 5. 19; Māl. 9. 48; so मदन, ˚भय, ˚शोक˚
&c.
--2 Loaded (as with a burden);
भाराक्रांता वसुंधरा Mk. 8. 6; K. 118;
Amaru. 30.
--3 Surpassed, eclipsed,
superseded; R. 10. 38, Ve. 5,
M. 3. 5.
--4 Obtained, possessed of;
[]
वर्णांतराक्रांतपयोधराग्रां R. 14. 27;
Ki. 11. 7.
--5 Accompanied, attended.
--6
Pained, distressed.

आक्रंदिन् a. Calling out in a
weeping tone, weeping, shouting at;
Ku. 5. 26.
